2026-11-28T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2502) 'the h3-vr reaches vrchat with one gain stage each
 # uuid: 3713b1c7-99e3-50c1-9318-bd6eaabe0ab9
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l1
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-28T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2502) 'a Zoom H3-VR used as the VRChat microphone, with each gain stage set once and named.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2502) 'the voice chain from the H3-VR's own gain to what other people in VRChat hear: the recorder, the Windows device, VRChat's input, gate and noise suppression.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2502) 'Can a 360 audio recorder be a VRChat microphone that sounds clear without a person guessing at five different volume knobs?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2502) 'The chain has five places that change loudness or remove sound: the recorder's gain, the Windows device level, VRChat's output mic level, VRChat's mic gate and VRChat's noise suppression. Set wrong, two of them fight. A gate that is too high cuts the start of words. Noise suppression on a good microphone eats the voice it was meant to keep. A device level and a recorder gain both low push the signal down into the noise floor, and both high clip it.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2502) 'Record the same spoken test line through the chain at the values below and at one changed value per stage. It passes when the line is heard whole, with no clipped peaks and no cut word starts, at the values below, and a single changed stage breaks at least one of those.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2502) 'the h3-vr reaches vrchat with one gain stage each
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The H3-VR's mic gain is 25 (operator, 2026-11-28).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The Windows microphone device level is 80 percent.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2502) '- VRChat's output mic level is 100.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2502) '- VRChat's mic gate is 2 percent.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2502) '- VRChat's noise suppression is off.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The H3-VR is in USB "Audio I/F" mode, "Stereo" (2-in/2-out, a stereo mix of its four inputs), not "4ch Ambisonics" (operator, 2026-11-28).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2502) '- These five values are the setting to start from, and a change to one of them is made one at a time and written here.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2502) '- H3-VR Operation Manual: https://zoomcorp.com/media/documents/E_H3-VR_2.pdf ("Using as an audio interface", page 80; "Adjusting input levels", page 37).
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Zoom H3-VR support: https://zoomcorp.com/en/ca/handheld-recorders/handheld-recorders/h3-vr-360-audio-recorder/h3-vr-support/
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2502) 'The chain
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2502) '| Stage | Where | Value |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2502) '| --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2502) '| Recorder gain | H3-VR mic gain | 25 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2502) '| Device level | Windows sound settings, the H3-VR as input | 80 percent |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2502) '| Output mic | VRChat audio settings | 100 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2502) '| Mic gate | VRChat audio settings | 2 percent |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2502) '| Noise suppression | VRChat audio settings | off |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2502) 'What the manual says
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Audio interface modes: "Stereo" sends inputs 1-4 as a stereo mix, 2-in/2-out, for Windows and Mac, on USB bus power. "4ch Ambisonics" sends the four converted tracks, 4-in/2-out, and on Windows needs the driver from ZOOM's website. "Stereo (iOS)" is for iOS devices.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Over USB 2.0 High Speed the interface runs 44.1 or 48 kHz at 24 bit. Full Speed is 16 bit.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Mic gain is +18 to +48 dB. The manual says to adjust so peaks on the level meters stay around -12 dBFS, and to lower the gain if the clipping indicator lights. It does not say what 25 on the dial is in dB.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The recorder has its own Lo Cut (10 to 240 Hz or off) and limiter. Neither is in the chain above, and both change the voice before VRChat hears it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Direct Monitor and Loop Back are audio interface settings. Loop Back mixes the computer's playback into what is sent back, so it must be off or other people hear themselves. It cannot be used in "4ch Ambisonics".
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The manual's loudness rule is peaks at -12 dBFS, so the gain of 25 is tested against that and not taken as right.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2502) 'Why each value
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The mode is "Stereo" because it is the one that needs no driver on Windows and gives the fewest channels. VRChat takes only a mono microphone (operator, 2026-11-28), so the two channels are made into one somewhere between the recorder and VRChat. Which stage does that is not known. "4ch Ambisonics" would send four channels and needs a driver on Windows. Not tested with it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Noise suppression is off because the recorder already gives a clean signal and suppression changes the voice. Not measured here.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The gate is 2 percent so it opens on quiet speech and still closes on silence. Not measured here.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2502) '- The device level is 80 percent and not 100 so the Windows stage has room before clipping. Not measured here.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2502) 'What was measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2502) 'Nothing yet. The values were read out from a working setup by the operator on 2026-11-28. The test in the exit line is not run.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2502) 'What is not known
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2502) '- What gain 25 is in dB, and whether its peaks sit near -12 dBFS on a spoken line.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Where the stereo mix becomes the one channel VRChat uses (the Windows device or VRChat), and whether the two channels cancel or add on a spoken line.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Lo Cut, limiter and Loop Back settings in use.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Whether the same values hold in a quiet room and a loud one.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2502) '- Whether the gate at 2 percent opens on room noise when the recorder gain is 25.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2502) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-28T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2502) 'The values live in a chat message. The next person with an H3-VR starts from nothing.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2502  1 LINE
 Text:Written

